---
/**
 * About, EN. Twin of `src/pages/a-propos.astro`.
 *
 * Describes the SERVICE and the EDITORIAL METHOD, never a company history:
 * there is no company (rule 1).
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { pathFor } from '@lib/routes.ts';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '@lib/schema.ts';

const locale = 'en' as const;
const ref = { type: 'static', page: 'about' } as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  ref={ref}
  title="About — how this referral service works"
  description="This site explains foundation problems in the Quebec City region and refers you to a licensed contractor. Here is how it is written and how it is funded."
  schema={[
    breadcrumbSchema(locale, [
      { name: "Home", ref: { type: 'home' } },
      { name: "About", ref },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <section class="contenant bloc-page">
    <div class="mesure">
      <h1>About Solage Capitale</h1>

      <p class="chapeau">
        Solage Capitale is an information site about residential foundations in the Quebec City
        region, paired with a referral service to a licensed contractor. It is not a
        construction company, and this page says so rather than leaving you to work it out.
      </p>

      <h2>What the service does</h2>
      <p>
        It answers the question that comes before all the others: <em>what is going on under my
        house, and who do I call?</em> Every page starts from a real problem — a drain that no
        longer carries water, a crack that is opening, water coming in during the spring melt —
        and explains the phenomenon, the regulations that apply, and what a professional does.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you request a quote, the request goes to an independent company holding its own
        licence from the Régie du bâtiment du Québec. That company visits, prices the work and
        performs it. <strong>Solage Capitale does not touch your foundation.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>How the content is written</h2>
      <p>
        Three rules, applied without exception, which explain what you will not find here.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No figure without a public source.</strong> Where no primary source publishes
          a range, the site says there is none rather than repeating a competitor's number. That
          is the case for prices, and the
          <a href={pathFor({ type: 'static', page: 'pricing' }, locale)}>pricing page</a>
          explains why.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No invented trust markers.</strong> No reviews, no star ratings, no
          testimonials, no "serving you since 19XX", no job-site photo presented as our own. The
          site's few photographs come from freely licensed archives and their provenance is
          recorded.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No execution instructions.</strong> The site explains what a professional
          does; it never tells you how to do it. A badly run excavation against a foundation
          injures people or destroys buildings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the site encourages you to do</h2>
      <p>
        Verify. Quebec's regulations are public and the licence register is open to anyone.
        Asking for the licence number, checking that it covers the right subcategory, and
        requiring the quote to name the standard used are steps that cost nothing and change the
        conversation. The <a href={pathFor({ type: 'static', page: 'faq' }, locale)}>frequently
        asked questions</a> explain how.
      </p>

      <h2>How the service is funded</h2>
      <p>
        By the contractor who receives the enquiries, not by you. Reading the site and asking
        for a quote are free and commit you to nothing. You remain free to seek other quotes —
        and doing so is recommended.
      </p>

      <h2>Service area</h2>
      <p>
        The Quebec City Metropolitan Community: the city's boroughs, Lévis, the surrounding
        municipalities and the neighbourhoods. The full list is on the
        <a href={pathFor({ type: 'static', page: 'serviceArea' }, locale)}>service area</a>
        page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
